   "source": ["# 05 — Churn Prediction\n", "Predict customer inactivity using classification models."]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["import json\n", "import pandas as pd\n", "from pathlib import Path\n", "\n", "PROCESSED = Path('..') / 'data' / 'processed'\n", "report = json.loads((PROCESSED / 'churn_report.json').read_text())\n", "report"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Model Comparison"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["comparison = pd.DataFrame(report['results']).T\n", "comparison"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Best Model"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["print(f'Best model: {report[\"best_model\"]}')\n", "best = report['results'][report['best_model']]\n", "for metric, value in best.items():\n", "    print(f'  {metric}: {value}')]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Feature Importance"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["fi = pd.DataFrame(\n", "    list(report['feature_importance'].items()),\n", "    columns=['Feature', 'Importance']\n", ").sort_values('Importance', ascending=False)\n", "\n", "import plotly.express as px\n", "px.bar(fi, x='Feature', y='Importance', title='XGBoost Feature Importance')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## SHAP Explanations"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": ["explain_path = PROCESSED / 'churn_explainability.json'\n", "if explain_path.exists():\n", "    shap_report = json.loads(explain_path.read_text())\n", "    print('Global SHAP Feature Importance:')\n", "    for row in shap_report['global_feature_importance'][:5]:\n", "        print(f'  {row[\"feature\"]}: {row[\"mean_abs_shap\"]:.4f}')\n", "else:\n", "    print('Run explain.py to generate SHAP explanations')"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## Churn Definition\n", "\n", "- **Churned** = no purchase in 90+ days relative to last date in dataset\n", "- Churn rate is approximately 33%\n", "- **Top predictive features**: days_since_last, recency, monetary\n", "- XGBoost outperforms Logistic Regression and Random Forest"]
  }
